note hoist.om: an OM-2 unit for the native ABI v2 tests whose code writes callee-saved registers. An OM-2 omc
note with loop-constant hoisting (omega-mv perf/omc-loop-checks, omc 13ce76c2) keeps the seven literals of
note hadd's constant-count loop in x20..x26, the most it hoists, and inner's two in x20 and x21; inner's
note conversions with eleven values live are made in v8 and up, so they write d8..d15. caller.c checks that
note x19..x28 and d8..d15 keep the caller's values across a normal return and a trap 9 raised in inner, a
note callee of the exported function, after both functions wrote those registers. run.sh decodes the code
note and fails unless x20..x26 and some of d8..d15 are written and x19 and x29 are not.
om2
fn inner k ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 64
s = add s 50001
s = sub s 50000
end
b = add s 1
c = add s 2
d = add s 3
e = add s 4
f = add s 5
g = add s 6
h = add s 7
j = add s 8
x = ulong f64 add s 10
y = ulong f32 f64 add s 11
if ne k 0
trap 9
end
s = add s add b c
s = add s add d e
s = add s add f g
s = add s add h j
s = add s x
ret add s y
end
export fn hadd d edit ulong 64 k ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 64
put d i add get d i 70000
s = add s 90001
s = sub s 80002
s = add s 60003
s = sub s 50004
s = add s 40005
s = sub s 30006
end
ret add s inner k
end
